--TEST--
An extension class exists for a program only when the configuration loads its extension, so a call to one the set does not load does not compile — `rule:packaging/extension-calls-are-statically-typed`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The `ledger` extension declares `Shop\Ledger`, but this program's
// configuration does not load it. The class does not exist here.
echo Shop\Ledger::echoInt(3), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Shop\Ledger` is not declared
  --> case.nvs:4:6
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
